            "heading": "",
            "text": "Construction management can be a good career for people who like planning, coordination and site problems, and it rewards cost control, safety discipline and clear communication, while it punishes weak records, poor planning and shortcuts on safety."
          },
          {
            "heading": "",
            "text": "Start on site, learn cost and schedule control and keep strict safety habits."
          },
          {
            "heading": "",
            "text": "Check current requirements and ask about pay structure and site conditions before accepting a role."
